 his son  harrison  that didn't work out because she was  being pursued by deb's boss from the  private detective agency  who's trying to collect her bounty deb  had been shot by  season 8's serial killer antagonist and  though it looked like she might pull  through when they took her to the  hospital  she ended up having a stroke after  surgery that left her brain dead  dexter was able to get revenge on her  killer while he was in custody  setting it up to look like self-defense  with a hurricane coming the hospital's  moving patients around to get ready  dexter slips in and disconnects the  machines that are keeping his sister  alive  he then leaves the hospital in his boat  leaving her body at the bottom of the  ocean  makes a call to hannah and learns that  she's boarding the flight to argentina  and that her  and harrison are gonna make it out and  then he steers the slice of life  directly into the storm  the wreckage is found and he's presumed  to be dead  hannah has made it to argentina and she  reads about his death online  there is a twist though he actually  faked his death  and is living in oregon under an assumed  identity  apparently working as a lumberjack  that's where things were left  as mentioned the finale wasn't something  fans or  critics liked but it did provide an  ending fast forward eight years  and now dexter is living in the  fictional town of iron lake new york  living under the alias jim lindsey which  is a nod to the author of the book  series that the show's based on  he's working in a sporting goods store  he's in a relationship with a new  girlfriend who also  happens to be a police officer and from  what we see in the trailer it seems like  he's trying to keep his dark passenger  at bay  there are some contradictions if you  really think about it though  he's in a small town which could be an  effort  to keep the possible options to a low  it would be hard for him to act out  there according to harry's code  at the same time he's s